  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Run a seeded Monte Carlo simulation of the ASI-PLC Compliance Bit state machine over a chosen mix of valid, non-compliant, MitM, replay and timeout scenarios, then check that it never permits a bad weld, that valid-weld latency stays under the 500 ms window, and how the scenarios split across PLC states. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
